Subject: telnet/telnetd: include <term.h> for tgetent() with ncurses

In the HAVE_CURSES_TGETENT branch, telnet.c and telnetd/utility.c
include <curses.h> and pull in <term.h> only when _XOPEN_CURSES is
not defined, assuming an X/Open curses declares tgetent() in
<curses.h> itself.  ncurses defines _XOPEN_CURSES but declares
tgetent() only in <term.h> (and <termcap.h>), so the call at
telnet.c:767 and utility.c:885 is left undeclared, which GCC 16
rejects:

    telnet.c:767:9: error: implicit declaration of function 'tgetent'

Include <term.h> unconditionally after <curses.h>.  ncurses's
<term.h> is meant to follow <curses.h>.

configure's own declaration probe carries the same guard, so it
reports "checking whether tgetent is declared... no" and leaves
HAVE_CURSES_TGETENT undefined; build.sh presets
ac_cv_have_decl_tgetent=yes to match.

---
diff -urN a/telnet/telnet.c b/telnet/telnet.c
--- a/telnet/telnet.c
+++ b/telnet/telnet.c
@@ -75,9 +75,7 @@
 # include <termcap.h>
 #elif defined HAVE_CURSES_TGETENT
 # include <curses.h>
-# ifndef _XOPEN_CURSES
-#  include <term.h>
-# endif
+# include <term.h>
 #endif
 
 #ifdef AUTHENTICATION
diff -urN a/telnetd/utility.c b/telnetd/utility.c
--- a/telnetd/utility.c
+++ b/telnetd/utility.c
@@ -39,9 +39,7 @@
 # include <termcap.h>
 #elif defined HAVE_CURSES_TGETENT
 # include <curses.h>
-# ifndef _XOPEN_CURSES
-#  include <term.h>
-# endif
+# include <term.h>
 #endif
 
 #if defined HAVE_STREAMSPTY && defined HAVE_GETMSG	\
